<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Success!!... here is what I did.<br>Downloaded and install the latest (OpenGD77CPSInstaller_R2025.02.03.01)<br>Using OpenGD77 CPS version R2025.02.03.01 <br><br>Downloaded and used the 210525 MD-9600 V4 firmware for PLL2571 (as the doner firmware).<br><br>Downloaded and used the OpenMDUV380.zip firmware (not the 10 Watt or GPS edition).<br>Did the firmware installation and screen now boots to VFO mode.<br><br>VA2PPZ is now very happy <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_wink.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=";-)" title="Wink"><br><br>Do we have a reference to how to set this radio back to calibrated values.<br>Or should I shay, back to 10Watts TX?<br><br>(ps), thank you for the immediate response &amp; suggestion.....it now works and others can take profit of this tribal knowledge.</div></blockquote>Go to Options -&gt; Radio Options and change Mode to 10W<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Fri Feb 28, 2025 3:02 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
