On January 30 2025, EB2BEP posted success with installing Opengd77 on a 390+ 10W (does not mention gps or not).<br>He also mentions having to use the Japanese edition of the firmware.<br><br>I want to report, that after having properly followed the instruction as per the original post on installation.<br>Neither firmware editions work on my 390+ (10w w/gps).<br>The radios behaviour after the installation with CPS ver. 2025-02 is the black screen.<br>Using the Opengd77 CPS, the radio info can be read..so there is communication.<br>I have also noticed writing (very very faint in the background of the black screen).<br><br>The exact credentials of my radio are as follows:<br>(Battery removed)<br>Model: MD-UV390 with orange plus sticker glued to the top right of the battery compartment.<br>serial number is : 2406BO01944<br><br>If anyone reading this has found a solution to this phenomena, do please share.<br>I will not be reverting back to OEM firmware for the next couple of days or weeks in hopes someone responds to this post.<br>73<br>Perry<br><br>edit: I've also backed up a copy of the registry BIN file to share, but cannot upload or attach it to this post.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7857">VA2PPZ</a> — Fri Feb 28, 2025 2:11 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
